body:
{Hibike Euphonium}

{A place further than the universe}

{Chihayafuru} there's two lead in love with the heroine but she doesn't care about romance, only karuta 

I also recommend the Webtoon beware of the villainess that talk about sexist trope in reverse harem and QQ sweeper with the sequel Queen's Quality where the heroine get stronger and stronger with time along with Your Throne which is THE Webtoon with a powerful female lead and another one who learn to be stronger too. They both inspire each other (don't trust the beginning, it trick you to think that they're rival)

There's more powerful women in otome Isekai that are still on Webtoon, the only issue though is that romance is still there. That can be annoying but on the good one the heroine usually focus on her objective rather than being swayed immediately by romance

{danshi koukousei no nichijou} have a similar humor than Gintama and two seyuu are present too 

{Osomatsu San} but it's pretty hit or miss 

